@startuml task-intake
!include state-machine-style.iuml
title Slop Machine | Task intake (FR-01 and FR-02)
caption Intake records an actionable task before it enters the scheduler queue. It holds no execution slot.

state Source <<choice>>
state "Query configured Jira backlog\nOr look up selected ticket key" as QueryJira
state "Select candidate ticket\nApply configured selection policy" as SelectTicket
state "Fetch Jira ticket\nRequirements, acceptance criteria, ID + revision" as FetchTicket
state "Record Jira-backed task\nPersist ticket link + source evidence" as RecordJira
state "Capture user prompt\nOriginal text + target project" as CapturePrompt
state "Assess prompt actionability\nPreserve prior clarifications" as AssessPrompt
state PromptDecision <<choice>>
state "Ask for missing information\nRecord question + task identity" as Ask
state "Await clarification\nNo slot or agent session" as WaitReply <<attention>>
state TrackingMode <<choice>>
state "Create Jira ticket from prompt\nVerify new key + link to request" as CreateTicket
state "Record prompt task\nInternal record or linked Jira ticket\nPreserve original request + answers" as RecordPrompt
state "Load existing task\nHuman review reply or explicit requeue" as ExistingTask
state "Ready to queue\nSource + project + tracking record saved" as Ready <<success>>
state "Idle intake\nNo eligible Jira candidate yet" as Idle
state "Needs attention\nRead/create failure or missing tracking policy" as Attention <<attention>>
state "Cancelled\nPrompt retained; no run started" as Cancelled <<attention>>

[*] --> Source
Source --> QueryJira : [Jira backlog or selected key]
Source --> CapturePrompt : [new user prompt]
Source --> ExistingTask : [existing task requeued]
QueryJira --> SelectTicket : candidate refs returned
QueryJira --> Idle : no candidate
QueryJira --> Attention : Jira read failed after recovery
SelectTicket --> FetchTicket : candidate chosen
FetchTicket --> RecordJira : ticket ID, revision + content captured
FetchTicket --> Attention : fetch failed after recovery
RecordJira --> Ready : task/ticket link persisted
CapturePrompt --> AssessPrompt : original request + project recorded
AssessPrompt --> PromptDecision : actionability assessed
PromptDecision --> Ask : [missing or conflicting information]
PromptDecision --> TrackingMode : [actionable]
Ask --> WaitReply : clarification request recorded
WaitReply --> AssessPrompt : reply received / append answer
WaitReply --> Cancelled : user cancels
TrackingMode --> CreateTicket : [configured Jira tracking]
TrackingMode --> RecordPrompt : [configured internal tracking]
TrackingMode --> Attention : no valid tracking policy
CreateTicket --> RecordPrompt : ticket created + linked + verified
CreateTicket --> Attention : creation unconfirmed after recovery
RecordPrompt --> Ready : tracking record verified
ExistingTask --> Ready : cause + task identity loaded
Idle --> [*] : return idle; retry on new input
Ready --> [*] : return queue_ready
Attention --> [*] : return attention
Cancelled --> [*] : return cancelled

note right of TrackingMode
  Prompt-to-ticket conversion before normal execution is optional
  under an explicit tracking policy. A prompt kept internally must
  acquire a linked original Jira ticket if FR-10 handoff is needed.
  See dependency-handoff.puml; preserve the original prompt origin.
end note
note bottom of WaitReply
  Clarifications append to the original request.
  Silence cannot make a prompt actionable.
  Timeout/escalation policy remains to be defined.
end note
@enduml
